WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:14.518
When an adult is paid, income tax comes straight out of their pay. When you buy a snack, V A T is already inside the price. Both are taxes, but they work differently.

00:00:15.080 --> 00:00:26.344
A direct tax is paid on income or profits: income tax and business tax. An indirect tax is paid on spending: V A T, excise duties, customs duties and tariffs.

00:00:26.920 --> 00:00:33.456
Taxes are the government's main source of revenue. A question may ask you to add up just one group.

00:00:34.560 --> 00:00:45.456
Step one, label each tax direct or indirect. Here income tax and corporation tax are direct. V A T and excise duties are indirect.

00:00:46.040 --> 00:00:59.401
Step two, add only the group asked for, and write the sum. For indirect taxes: eighteen point five plus four point five is twenty-three. Step three, give the units: twenty-three billion pounds.

00:01:00.520 --> 00:01:15.616
Here is a real question from June 2024. A table lists five taxes in billions of pounds. Calculate the total revenue raised by indirect taxes. Two marks.

00:01:16.200 --> 00:01:26.901
Label each one. Income tax and business taxes are direct, so leave them out. Sales tax, excise duties and customs duties are indirect.

00:01:27.480 --> 00:01:40.004
Add them. Fourteen point three plus three point seven plus nought point four is eighteen point four billion pounds. This explanation is by olevels dot com, not an official mark scheme.

00:01:40.560 --> 00:01:47.449
Sales tax brings in most of it. The three bars together make eighteen point four billion.

00:01:48.560 --> 00:01:54.967
A common mistake is mixing the groups, such as adding income tax to V A T.

00:01:55.520 --> 00:01:59.985
Another is leaving out the units. Write billions of pounds.

00:02:01.120 --> 00:02:20.265
Now you try. Income tax raises forty-two billion pounds, V A T twenty-five point five, corporation tax eleven point two, fuel duty six point eight and tariffs one point five. Calculate total revenue from direct taxes. Pause here and work it out.

00:02:21.400 --> 00:02:31.791
Income tax and corporation tax are on income and profit, so they are direct. V A T, fuel duty and tariffs are on spending, so leave them out.

00:02:32.360 --> 00:02:39.962
Forty-two plus eleven point two is fifty-three point two. Total direct tax revenue is fifty-three point two billion pounds.

00:02:40.520 --> 00:02:48.391
Remember: label every tax, add only the group asked for, and keep the units. Now try the practice questions.
